# CLAUDE.md

This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.

## Project Overview

**Trackbliss** — React SPA for managing EU ESPR 2024/1781 Digital Product Passports (DPPs). Multi-tenant SaaS with Supabase backend, AI compliance analysis via Claude Sonnet 4, integrated Returns Hub (tickets + customer portal), warehouse + shipping module with smart packing engine, white-label custom domains, and DPP design system. UI in German + English. Production at https://dpp-app.fambliss.eu (Vercel auto-deploy on push to main).

## Commands

```bash
npm run dev          # Vite dev server
npm run build        # tsc -b && vite build
npm run lint         # ESLint (flat config)
npx tsc --noEmit     # Type-check only

# Migrations (require SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN + SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF in .env)
node scripts/db-migrate.mjs              # Apply all pending migrations
node scripts/db-migrate.mjs --status     # Show migration status
node scripts/db-migrate.mjs --file X.sql # Apply one specific migration

# Seeds (require SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY)
node scripts/seed-countries.mjs
node scripts/seed-checklist-templates.mjs
node scripts/seed-eu-regulations.mjs
node scripts/seed-news.mjs
node scripts/setup-storage.mjs
```

The migration runner uses the Supabase **Management API** (`POST /v1/projects/{ref}/database/query`) because the REST/PostgREST endpoint cannot execute DDL. Applied migrations are tracked in a `_migrations` table.

## Tech Stack

React 19 · TypeScript · Vite 7 · Tailwind 4 · shadcn/ui (New York style) · React Router 7 · Supabase (Postgres + Auth + Storage + RLS + Edge Functions) · `@tanstack/react-query` · `framer-motion` · `@react-pdf/renderer` · `jsbarcode` · `qrcode` · `cmdk` · `html5-qrcode` · Lucide icons · OpenRouter (Claude Sonnet 4) for AI. Hosting: Vercel.

## High-Level Architecture

### Context hierarchy (`App.tsx`)

```
BrowserRouter
  AuthProvider                      — session + tenantId from profiles table
    BillingProvider                 — entitlements, quotas, AI credits (loads on auth)
      BrandingProvider              — runtime theming via CSS vars + favicon + title
        CustomDomainGate            — checks hostname; swaps to slug-free routing
          CustomDomainPortal        — when hostname is a tenant's custom domain
          DomainNotFoundPage        — custom domain not resolved
          NormalAppRoutes           — standard /login, /p/…, /returns/…, /customer/…, etc.
            ProtectedRoute          — inline guard (not HOC); redirects unauth to /login
              AppLayout             — sidebar + header for authenticated pages
```

`CustomDomainGate` reads `window.location.hostname`, checks a `KNOWN_HOSTS` allowlist, otherwise queries `tenants.settings.returnsHub.portalDomain.customDomain` (anon RLS) to resolve the tenant. Result cached in sessionStorage.

### Multi-tenant isolation

Every tenant-scoped DB call **must** call `getCurrentTenantId()` (from `src/lib/supabase.ts`) first. This reads `tenant_id` from `profiles` (linked to `auth.users`). All tenant tables enforce RLS policies checking `tenant_id = (SELECT tenant_id FROM profiles WHERE id = auth.uid())`.

### Service layer convention

- All DB/Storage access goes through `src/services/supabase/*`. Never call `supabase.from(...)` directly in components.
- Each service has a `transform*()` function at the boundary converting `snake_case` DB rows to `camelCase` TS objects (and the reverse on writes).
- Quota/billing enforcement uses **`await import('./billing')`** dynamic imports inside 12+ services (`products.ts`, `batches.ts`, `documents.ts`, `returns.ts`, `rh-tickets.ts`, etc.) to break the circular dependency that would exist if `billing.ts` loaded them at module top level.

