### Edge Functions (`supabase/functions/*`)

| Function | Trigger | Secrets needed |
|---|---|---|
| `send-email` | INSERT on `rh_notifications` (channel=email, status=pending) | `SMTP_HOST`, `SMTP_PORT`, `SMTP_USER`, `SMTP_PASS`, `SMTP_FROM` |
| `manage-vercel-domain` | HTTP from client (JWT + admin role) | `VERCEL_TOKEN`, `VERCEL_PROJECT_ID`, `VERCEL_TEAM_ID` |
| `create-checkout-session` | HTTP from client (JWT) | `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` |
| `create-portal-session` | HTTP from client (JWT) | `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` |
| `stripe-webhook` | Stripe webhook | `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` |

### Storage buckets (`supabase/storage.sql`)

| Bucket | Public | Max size | Path pattern |
|---|---|---|---|
| `documents` | No | 50 MB | `{tenantId}/{timestamp}-{rnd}.{ext}` |
| `product-images` | Yes | 10 MB | `{tenantId}/{productId}-{timestamp}.{ext}` |
| `branding` | Yes | 2 MB | `{tenantId}/{filename}` |
| `return-photos` | No | 50 MB | `{tenantId}/{filename}` |

RLS on all buckets checks `(storage.foldername(name))[1] = tenant_id::text` — so the first path segment **must** be the tenant ID.

## Smart Packing Assistant (carrier rule engine)

`lib/smart-packing.ts` + `lib/smart-packing-data.ts` encode the rules from `Kurier_Verpackungsregeln_Europa_v2.xlsx`:

- ~40 carrier services across 23 EU carriers (DHL, Hermes, DPD, GLS, UPS, FedEx, Royal Mail, PostNL, Colissimo, …) with per-service max weight, max dimensions, min label size, price-from values.
- 7 girth formulas (`l_plus_2b_2h`, `l_plus_2_bh`, `longest_plus_2bh`, `sum_3`, `perimeter_only`, `l_plus_girth`, `none`).
- 27 country zones with ISO-2, VAT, currency, eurozone flag, duties flag, country-specific hints (Canaries as 3rd country, UK Brexit/UKCA, NO VOEC, CH verzollungsgebühr, IT Codice Fiscale, ES Balearen, …).
- ~32 origin→dest routes × 5 weight tiers × 5 carriers (EUR/CHF/GBP) with linear interpolation for any weight between 2 and 30 kg.
- Customs forms (CN22 <2 kg + <€368, CN23 otherwise, EUR.1 above €10.300 preferential threshold, Commercial/Proforma Invoice).
- Incoterms 2020 with contextual tags (b2c / b2b / third_country / high_value).
- Transit times for 20 destinations from DE.
- Surcharges: oversize, heavy >25 kg, Saturday, timed slot, age check, COD, customs clearance, fuel %, peak season (Nov–Jan), island, address correction.
- PPWR deadlines 2026/2028/2029/2030.

`SmartPackingCard.tsx` consumes this. The card **computes weight from items itself** (sum of `grossWeight × quantity` + 400 g packaging tare) if the form `packageWeightKg` prop is 0, and includes an auto-detected unit-mismatch warning if any single item > 50 kg/unit (catches g↔kg confusion).

## Document versioning

Migration `20260418_document_versions.sql` adds a `document_versions` table. The `documents` row always represents the **current** version; `document_versions` is the immutable history. Each `uploadDocumentVersion()`:

1. Uploads new file to storage (`{tenantId}/{ts}-{rnd}.{ext}`).
2. Inserts a new `document_versions` row with `version_number = MAX + 1`.
3. Updates the `documents` row's `storage_path`, `size`, `type`, `uploaded_at`, `uploaded_by` to point at the new file.

`restoreDocumentVersion()` reuses the old blob path (no copy); `deleteDocument()` must collect storage paths from all versions before deleting, because `ON DELETE CASCADE` removes only DB rows, not storage blobs.

## Conventions & Gotchas

- **Weight units**: Product `gross_weight` / `net_weight` are stored in **grams**. Convert `/1000` at the boundary when feeding into smart-packing (which works in kg). This has caused real bugs; see `CreateShipmentPage.tsx:resolvedItems` and `wh-stock.ts:transformStockLevel`.
- **Component identity**: Don't define wrapper components (e.g., a `Section` layout component) **inside** another function component. React re-creates them on every render → entire subtree unmounts → inputs lose focus on every keystroke. Define them at module scope. Caused a real bug on the recipient search in `CreateShipmentPage`.
- **iOS Safari camera**: `getUserMedia` must be called synchronously from the user gesture window. `CameraScannerView` warms up with `navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia` in the same tick as the click handler, THEN hands off to `html5-qrcode`. Don't use `{ facingMode: { exact: 'environment' } }` — iOS rejects it. Use `{ ideal: 'environment' }` for warm-up; pass plain string `{ facingMode: 'environment' }` to html5-qrcode (it rejects `{ ideal }`).
- **Barcode rendering**: Master Label Editor uses `jsbarcode` in both the preview (renders as SVG into a `<svg ref>`) and the PDF export (paints onto offscreen canvas → PNG data URL → `<Image src>` in `@react-pdf/renderer`). Invalid formats (e.g., non-numeric EAN-13) show an inline error rather than produce an unscannable code.
- **Auto-fill pattern**: In multi-step forms, auto-fill effects should only run when the target field is empty, so manual edits are never overwritten. If the user clears the field, the auto-fill re-suggests. See `CreateShipmentPage.tsx:useEffect` for weight/carrier/cost/ETA.
- **Tenant settings JSONB**: Branding, Returns Hub config, QR settings, DPP design, supplier portal, portal domain all live in `tenants.settings` (JSONB). Only billing lives in dedicated `billing_*` tables.
- **Product dimensions with batch fallback**: When computing package dimensions, the convention is `product.productDepthCm ?? batch.productDepthCm` (and likewise for weight). Products set master values; batches can override per batch.
- **GTIN search deep-link**: Scanner's "Product not found" prompt navigates to `/products/new?gtin=…`. `ProductFormPage` reads `useSearchParams()` to pre-fill the GTIN field.

## i18n

Namespaces loaded at runtime from `public/locales/{en,de}/{ns}.json` via `i18next-http-backend`. Key conventions:

- Use the English text as the key: `t('Save')`, not `t('save_button')`.
- Cross-namespace access: `t('Cancel', { ns: 'common' })`.
- Interpolation: `t('Welcome {{name}}', { name })`.
- When adding any UI string, update **both** `en` and `de` files in the same commit. There is no English fallback automation — missing German keys render the English literal.

Namespaces: `common`, `auth`, `products`, `dpp`, `documents`, `dashboard`, `settings`, `compliance`, `returns`, `customer-portal`, `landing`, `supplier-portal`, `billing`, `legal`, `warehouse`.

## Environment Variables

```env
# Frontend (Vite)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxx.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...
VITE_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...  # optional — AI compliance

# Server-side scripts
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...   # seeds only
SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=sbp_...       # migrations (Management API)
SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=xxxxxxxxxx

# Edge Function secrets — set in Supabase dashboard
SMTP_HOST / SMTP_PORT / SMTP_USER / SMTP_PASS / SMTP_FROM
VERCEL_TOKEN / VERCEL_PROJECT_ID / VERCEL_TEAM_ID
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY / STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET
```

## Routing quick-map

| Path prefix | Auth | Layout |
|---|---|---|
| `/login`, `/landing`, `/auth/*` | None | Bare |
| `/p/:gtin/:serial`, `/01/:gtin/21/:serial` | None | `PublicLayout` |
| `/suppliers/register/:code` | None | Bare (invitation-validated) |
| `/returns/portal/:slug`, `/returns/register/:slug`, `/returns/track` | None | Portal |
| `/customer/:slug/*` | Separate customer auth | `CustomerPortalProvider` |
| (any other custom-domain path) | Depends | `CustomDomainPortal` (slug-free) |
| Everything else | `ProtectedRoute` | `AppLayout` (sidebar + header) |
